WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.367
Cut A4 paper in half.

2
00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:04.000
Turn it.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.367
It’s almost the same
shape, only smaller.

4
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:09.700
A square cannot do that.

5
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:12.767
Halve it, and you get
a skinny rectangle.

6
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:16.900
A-series paper is built
around a special ratio:

7
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.367
one to the
square root of two.

8
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:21.800
Halve the long side,

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
then rotate the piece.

10
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.533
That ratio comes back.

11
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
In the ideal system,

12
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.900
an A3 design shrinks to A4
without stretching.

13
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.500
Each length shrinks to about
seventy-one percent.

14
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:38.700
The area halves.

15
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.067
Real paper sizes are rounded
to whole millimetres.

16
00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:46.533
The perfect rule lives
in the geometry.

17
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.733
Half the paper.

18
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.867
Same proportions.
